 "geometry_notes": [
  "Origin at mid-soffit, y up. Outline built in cm and scaled to mm.",
  "Closed void: printed top width, bottom width, height and chamfer runs; chamfers taken at 45° (drawn 45°, rise not printed).",
  "Inner web face passes through the two chamfer end points; outer web face is offset by the printed web thickness (9 cm; B-400 17 cm) measured NORMAL to the web (the CA-150/180/B-400 dimension lines are drawn perpendicular to the web; horizontal and normal differ by <0.1 cm here).",
  "Soffit corners: tangent arc R5 (B-400: R40) between the soffit and the outer web line. B-400 R40 is not printed; it was measured from the vector drawing (circle through the drawn tangent points (43.1,0) and (82.8,35.3) cm gives R=39.97 cm) and agrees with the printed 86.3 flat / 35.3 arc-height / 165.7 base.",
  "Upper web–wing junction: tangent arc R22 (B-400: R20). The wing soffit line passes through the tip at a_max (tip thickness b=5) and its slope is solved so that the fillet's wing tangent point lies b1 (7.8; B-400 7.1) below the tip soffit, i.e. the printed 5 + b1 + 20.2 (17.6) chain. The resulting web-tangent height is compared with the printed straight-web height.",
  "Wing widths below a_max: tip moves inward along the fixed wing soffit line (catalogue b+b1 is constant for every row).",
  "Drip notches, lifting inserts, shear keys and the small leader-line artefacts in the drawing fill are omitted.",
  "CA-135 closed drawing prints a=300 cm while its table and overview use 310 cm; a_max=310 is used (the table governs; the drawing width is a known source inconsistency).",
  "CA-180 closed drawing prints a 147.2 cm straight web (147.2+20.2+7.8+5 = 180.2); the Type U drawing prints 147. The fillet solution gives the value reported in residuals.",
  "Type U (first stage): same outer profile. Wing ends at gap/2 + stub (printed 7 cm; B-400 12 cm) and drops to the closed-void top level, where a ledge runs inward to gap/2. CA Type U: a 45° chamfer runs from that ledge edge down to the inner web face, which is offset by the printed U web thickness (11 cm; B-400 15 cm) from the outer web; the inner bottom corners are tangent arcs of radius 27 cm (NOT printed; measured from the vector drawing of CA-135-U, CA-150-U and CA-180-U, all ~27 cm) to the printed 20/20/25 cm bottom slab. B-400 Type U: vertical face at gap/2 down to a 45° chamfer whose line x+y=206.1 cm was measured from the drawing, then the web; bottom corners are the closed-box 25 cm 45° chamfers relative to the U web face. The small (~1.5 cm) rounding at the stub bottom corner is omitted.",
  "CA-150-U/CA-180-U chains close to 309.8/310 cm; gap/2 + stub is used for the wing end (0.1 cm closure error on CA-150-U).",
  "Source table anomalies retained verbatim: TC180 Type U a=190 repeats 7280 cm2 (a=200)."
 ],
